(3419137, 477106, 67844, '<td valign="top">I like the cloud and the rural area. A little more cloud on the sides would be nice and maybe a bit more blue sky on top.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-03-08 01:08:42.</i></td>', 'I like the cloud and the rural area. A little more cloud on the sides would be nice and maybe a bit more blue sky on top.', '2007-03-01 15:14:21.000000', '2007-03-08 01:08:42.000000', 1),
(3419150, 467416, 27087, '<td valign="top">good action shot 8</td>', 'good action shot 8', '2007-03-01 15:18:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3419155, 477103, 60173, '<td valign="top">Someone once told me about colors vs emotion. When you see snow your mind says "cold." So to prevent a mental conflict you want to stay in the cool area of the color wheel. I agree with that to a point. With solo pictures I''d agree. If you''re making a collection and the whole collection is going to make a statement then I''d say you can wander off in whatever color direction you want.<br/> <br/>In this case I''m not really digging the red. Red + water = blood. If your intent was to make the poor ducks swimming in blood then I guess you accomplished your goal. However I''m not sure that was your intent, so I would have suggested using a cool blue/purple/grey. I struggle sometimes with choosing colors like this. The red certainly does look cool on certain elements of the photo, but as a whole it doesn''t completely work.</td>', 'Someone once told me about colors vs emotion. When you see snow your mind says "cold." So to prevent a mental conflict you want to stay in the cool area of the color wheel. I agree with that to a point. With solo pictures I''d agree. If you''re making a collection and the whole collection is going to make a statement then I''d say you can wander off in whatever color direction you want. In this case I''m not really digging the red. Red + water = blood. If your intent was to make the poor ducks swimming in blood then I guess you accomplished your goal. However I''m not sure that was your intent, so I would have suggested using a cool blue/purple/grey. I struggle sometimes with choosing colors like this. The red certainly does look cool on certain elements of the photo, but as a whole it doesn''t completely work.', '2007-03-01 15:19:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(3419157, 474545, 66952, '<td valign="top">You''ve captured the peacefulness of the place very well. Taking pictures basically into the sun like this is hard, because the sky gets totally blown out, while the stuff on the ground is still too dark.</td>', 'You''ve captured the peacefulness of the place very well. Taking pictures basically into the sun like this is hard, because the sky gets totally blown out, while the stuff on the ground is still too dark.', '2007-03-01 15:19:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3419158, 475495, 27087, '<td valign="top">Well done, love the lighting 8</td>', 'Well done, love the lighting 8', '2007-03-01 15:19:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(3419162, 476696, 27087, '<td valign="top">B&amp;W done right good work 8</td>', 'B&W done right good work 8', '2007-03-01 15:20:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3419163, 477191, 6999, '<td valign="top">I just don''t get the use of colour for images like this: to my eye, it removes all sense of dynamic, of action, of expression. It becomes clinical, too carefully observed and selected, cold, in the end, meaningless. The light is, of course, dreadful - as in any kind of sports hall situation.<br/> <br/>I know it''s actually a very strong action photograph: perhaps I just don''t have the slightest interest in action photographs. Whatever the reason, I actively dislike this image, and I''m struggling to know why. Something here doesn''t engage me, for sure - I''m wondering if that is simply the light, the flatness, featurelessness of it, the fact that the background is just as bright as your subjects, the lack of sense of contrast in light. The composition, framing, upsets me too - the available space image left seems to dismiss the presence of the green figure, almost telling me to focus entirely on the power, the sense of success, the aggressor in the girl shooting; almost as though the girl in green were incidental, only included to avoid cropping some part of her body out of the image. I don''t understand.<br/> <br/>Just don''t understand.</td>', 'I just don''t get the use of colour for images like this: to my eye, it removes all sense of dynamic, of action, of expression. It becomes clinical, too carefully observed and selected, cold, in the end, meaningless. The light is, of course, dreadful - as in any kind of sports hall situation. I know it''s actually a very strong action photograph: perhaps I just don''t have the slightest interest in action photographs. Whatever the reason, I actively dislike this image, and I''m struggling to know why. Something here doesn''t engage me, for sure - I''m wondering if that is simply the light, the flatness, featurelessness of it, the fact that the background is just as bright as your subjects, the lack of sense of contrast in light. The composition, framing, upsets me too - the available space image left seems to dismiss the presence of the green figure, almost telling me to focus entirely on the power, the sense of success, the aggressor in the girl shooting; almost as though the girl in green were incidental, only included to avoid cropping some part of her body out of the image. I don''t understand. Just don''t understand.', '2007-03-01 15:20:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3419184, 477200, 27087, '<td valign="top">very cool shot 9</td>', 'very cool shot 9', '2007-03-01 15:26:13.000000', NULL, 1),
