(3442110, 473095, 37845, '<td valign="top">The model is a friend of mine, and a mother of two believe it or not. <br/> <br/>The strange shadows in the background are left there in error, and can only be seen when yor monitor is really bright. That is the only thing I regret about the photo.<br/> <br/>Any silicon that is in the photo is not somthing I can contol, so its unfortunate that some people felt it took away from the photo. Im not a professional photographer, and do not have access to a bevy of models (though i am working towards that :)  Also, I hope that people where not offended by a nude image, if they were I would have preferred they skip voting on this image, rather than giving it a low rating. <br/> <br/>I got this by using the colour select tool to select the yellow, inverting the selection, and desaturating the image using the channel mixer. The background is just black fabric i bought at a fabric store. Because there were different fabric types, i had to burn some of it in PS, and on my monitor it appeared fine. Only when i increased the brightness/contrast on my monitor did i see the shadows that i referred to earlier.<br/> <br/>Although I am dissappionted with how the photo performed, I will take consolation in the fact that I had twice as many views during the competition as the winners... they clearly were the best photos, but being popular is nice too :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-03-08 06:38:34.</i></td>', 'The model is a friend of mine, and a mother of two believe it or not.  The strange shadows in the background are left there in error, and can only be seen when yor monitor is really bright. That is the only thing I regret about the photo. Any silicon that is in the photo is not somthing I can contol, so its unfortunate that some people felt it took away from the photo. Im not a professional photographer, and do not have access to a bevy of models (though i am working towards that :)  Also, I hope that people where not offended by a nude image, if they were I would have preferred they skip voting on this image, rather than giving it a low rating.  I got this by using the colour select tool to select the yellow, inverting the selection, and desaturating the image using the channel mixer. The background is just black fabric i bought at a fabric store. Because there were different fabric types, i had to burn some of it in PS, and on my monitor it appeared fine. Only when i increased the brightness/contrast on my monitor did i see the shadows that i referred to earlier. Although I am dissappionted with how the photo performed, I will take consolation in the fact that I had twice as many views during the competition as the winners... they clearly were the best photos, but being popular is nice too :)', '2007-03-08 06:22:38.000000', '2007-03-08 06:38:34.000000', 0),
