(3443087, 477202, 10390, '<td valign="top">wow... a good translating job waiting for me when I get home tonight from school/work... no she doesn\''t understand english good enough to read or write herself but I have been translating for her and the work continues... A great pleasant job it is.. She tells me what to write and I translate it for her to english (as good as I can).<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SandyP:</b></div><hr/><i> Gasp!!!  First because of this spectacular photo. . then:  9 years old!  How can anyone obtain such talent in only 9 years, especially when the first few were learning things like walking, taling. . .and ENGLISH!   YOU, Miss ArnaRos are a prodigy!  <br/> <br/>CONGRATULATIONS on your first of MANY ribbons I\''m sure.   Look out Iceland. . .the pressure is on to be even better than EVER!<br/> <br/>In wonder:  Is Dad happy to the core????  Orrrr....ummm. . .a bit jealous?  :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Of course I\''m happy, she is amazing!  And who wouldn\''t be jealous of her with a photo like this!  We took some 2-3 hours one night in the end of February to take some photos together because neither of us had taken many photographs in February and both of us want to take part in all of the free study challenges this year. I have to admit that my photos weren\''t as good as hers that we took that night, we picked some 20 photos to choose from and then she picked out this one of this bridge.. yes she\''s talented for sure and we parents are very proud! Thanks!</td>', 'wow... a good translating job waiting for me when I get home tonight from school/work... no she doesn\''t understand english good enough to read or write herself but I have been translating for her and the work continues... A great pleasant job it is.. She tells me what to write and I translate it for her to english (as good as I can). Originally posted by SandyP: Gasp!!!  First because of this spectacular photo. . then:  9 years old!  How can anyone obtain such talent in only 9 years, especially when the first few were learning things like walking, taling. . .and ENGLISH!   YOU, Miss ArnaRos are a prodigy!   CONGRATULATIONS on your first of MANY ribbons I\''m sure.   Look out Iceland. . .the pressure is on to be even better than EVER! In wonder:  Is Dad happy to the core????  Orrrr....ummm. . .a bit jealous?  :)   Of course I\''m happy, she is amazing!  And who wouldn\''t be jealous of her with a photo like this!  We took some 2-3 hours one night in the end of February to take some photos together because neither of us had taken many photographs in February and both of us want to take part in all of the free study challenges this year. I have to admit that my photos weren\''t as good as hers that we took that night, we picked some 20 photos to choose from and then she picked out this one of this bridge.. yes she\''s talented for sure and we parents are very proud! Thanks!', '2007-03-08 12:14:41.000000', NULL, 0),
