(3445663, 469748, 23484, '<td valign="top">This is a lot harder to do than it looks. I know because I tried it. I like the colors. Why did you have such a long exposure?</td>', 'This is a lot harder to do than it looks. I know because I tried it. I like the colors. Why did you have such a long exposure?', '2007-03-09 07:58:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3445668, 477502, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very beautiful shot. I agree with your notes about the eye contact.</td>', 'Very beautiful shot. I agree with your notes about the eye contact.', '2007-03-09 08:03:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3445677, 477210, 23484, '<td valign="top">I think this is a decent shot. It has that uncomfortable feel of a rough winter and the snowstorm really adds to that feeling. I think you captured it well.</td>', 'I think this is a decent shot. It has that uncomfortable feel of a rough winter and the snowstorm really adds to that feeling. I think you captured it well.', '2007-03-09 08:09:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3445679, 471544, 23484, '<td valign="top">Jeffrey, you are the master of the monuments. I think this is well composed and the lighting is very nice. At first, I didn''t like the slow shutter speed causing the flag movement but the more I think about it, I believe it was a good choice.</td>', 'Jeffrey, you are the master of the monuments. I think this is well composed and the lighting is very nice. At first, I didn''t like the slow shutter speed causing the flag movement but the more I think about it, I believe it was a good choice.', '2007-03-09 08:11:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3445698, 471853, 11854, '<td valign="top">Take a long walk off a short pier. Suicide by drowning. Hypothermic. Pain for only an instant, than fade away.  Wow! Very thought provoking. Dark, mysterious. I love it!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-03-09 10:02:35.</i></td>', 'Take a long walk off a short pier. Suicide by drowning. Hypothermic. Pain for only an instant, than fade away.  Wow! Very thought provoking. Dark, mysterious. I love it!', '2007-03-09 08:27:23.000000', '2007-03-09 10:02:35.000000', 0),
(3445734, 470413, 66597, '<td valign="top">I absolutely love these bearded dragons, and this is a great capture. The colors are beautiful, and he''s definitely showing some attitude here :-)</td>', 'I absolutely love these bearded dragons, and this is a great capture. The colors are beautiful, and he''s definitely showing some attitude here :-)', '2007-03-09 08:52:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3445738, 476480, 66597, '<td valign="top">Deb, this has a wonderful perspective and great relative size of the woman vs. the window. I''m not sure about the crop, but I do admit that the curtains in the top window enhance the green in the shutters well, so I can certainly see why you chose to include it.</td>', 'Deb, this has a wonderful perspective and great relative size of the woman vs. the window. I''m not sure about the crop, but I do admit that the curtains in the top window enhance the green in the shutters well, so I can certainly see why you chose to include it.', '2007-03-09 08:54:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3445891, 477402, 36981, '<td valign="top">I''m going through my favorite photos in this challenge &amp; can''t believe that this scored as low as I did.  It was definitely in my top 20.  I think it''s a beautiful image; I love the noise, the title, the spacing of the heads, etc.  I''m sorry that others didn''t agree, but wanted you to know that someone thinks it''s great!</td>', 'I''m going through my favorite photos in this challenge & can''t believe that this scored as low as I did.  It was definitely in my top 20.  I think it''s a beautiful image; I love the noise, the title, the spacing of the heads, etc.  I''m sorry that others didn''t agree, but wanted you to know that someone thinks it''s great!', '2007-03-09 10:08:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3445897, 475421, 36981, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorite images, and I''m shocked that it didn''t score/place better.  I think it''s a fabulous portrait. EstimatedEyes said it all for me below.  For me, this really stood out in the competition!</td>', 'This was one of my favorite images, and I''m shocked that it didn''t score/place better.  I think it''s a fabulous portrait. EstimatedEyes said it all for me below.  For me, this really stood out in the competition!', '2007-03-09 10:10:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3445904, 469748, 70828, '<td valign="top">... because I opened the shutter in an almost blackened room then dropped the lemon and flashed an outboard strobe by hand at the kerplunk ... all done manually ... :)</td>', '... because I opened the shutter in an almost blackened room then dropped the lemon and flashed an outboard strobe by hand at the kerplunk ... all done manually ... :)', '2007-03-09 10:11:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3445905, 475984, 36981, '<td valign="top">I''ve got to agree with the other post-commentators.  I was going through my photos in this competition, ranked by my vote, and couldn''t believe that this didn''t score really high.  I love the image - it''s original, adorable, shows personality and is technically really well done.  Sorry that more didn''t agree ...<br/> <br/>p.s. it was in my top ten at least :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-03-09 10:12:52.</i></td>', 'I''ve got to agree with the other post-commentators.  I was going through my photos in this competition, ranked by my vote, and couldn''t believe that this didn''t score really high.  I love the image - it''s original, adorable, shows personality and is technically really well done.  Sorry that more didn''t agree ... p.s. it was in my top ten at least :)', '2007-03-09 10:12:01.000000', '2007-03-09 10:12:52.000000', 0),
(3445921, 477202, 52572, '<td valign="top">Oh my...u are such a gifted for photography<br/>and i love ur works!! now u are in my fav!!</td>', 'Oh my...u are such a gifted for photographyand i love ur works!! now u are in my fav!!', '2007-03-09 10:21:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3446064, 474907, 30049, '<td valign="top">Great clarity and focus on this.  The white balance is pretty good, although the white has a slight cool (bluish) cast to it.  I''m wondering if you used flash on this - at first glance it would appear to be yes (glint in eye, slight glare on lower beak), but the shutter speed is throwing me off.  Would have thought the shutter speed to be higher than 1/60 - reduced for fill flash in low light situation perhaps?  :-)<br/> <br/>Compositionally I would have trimmed a bit off the left to try and bring the eye more to a ROT point.  Just a thought.<br/> <br/>I do have to say I''m a tad jealous of the location!  Hawaii, eh?  Nice.  Been there twice, last time in the last 80''s.<br/> <br/>I''m also a tad embarrassed to just now notice you''ve been tossing some challenge entries into the mix recently - I should know what my ''Fav'' photographers are up to!  :P<br/> <br/>Hope all is well with you.  Take care.</td>', 'Great clarity and focus on this.  The white balance is pretty good, although the white has a slight cool (bluish) cast to it.  I''m wondering if you used flash on this - at first glance it would appear to be yes (glint in eye, slight glare on lower beak), but the shutter speed is throwing me off.  Would have thought the shutter speed to be higher than 1/60 - reduced for fill flash in low light situation perhaps?  :-) Compositionally I would have trimmed a bit off the left to try and bring the eye more to a ROT point.  Just a thought. I do have to say I''m a tad jealous of the location!  Hawaii, eh?  Nice.  Been there twice, last time in the last 80''s. I''m also a tad embarrassed to just now notice you''ve been tossing some challenge entries into the mix recently - I should know what my ''Fav'' photographers are up to!  :P Hope all is well with you.  Take care.', '2007-03-09 11:16:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3446181, 477499, 5792, '<td valign="top">Positive:<br/>Overall this is a fine photojournalistic capture worthy of publication. This image has strong emotion. The BG provides perspective and context to the image far, far better than most. Exposure is good and general photographic technical quality is fine. It gives the viewer much to think about. Is this the wrestler''s father happy at a victory? Is it a coach happy over his first ever state champion? It preserves a touching moment in time that can never be captured again which is a fundamental purpose of photography itself.<br/> <br/>Technicals:<br/>The BG is a strength. It clearly shows the context generating the reaction we see. Inclusion of the referee is very nice and it clearly shows the gym atmosphere of a wrestling competition. You are perfectly placed for the capture of the moment. That makes this a very fine image.<br/> <br/>Though exposure is good the overall lighting is nothing special. The capture of the moment is great, but the overall perspective has more in common with a snapshot than it does with fine art.<br/> <br/>The challenge:<br/>Right or wrong, voters in free study challenges are looking more for fine art images of exceptional technical quality than anything else. The ''snapshot'' perspective and lack of funk and flash post processing hurt this image in voting. When there are over 600 entries in a challenge with many being exceptional technical achievements it is easy for an image like this to be overlooked. It was.<br/> <br/>If you had surrounded it with a gradient like the three ribbon winners and applied some serious dodge and burn to hit the voter over the head with the embrace then it would have been more ''artistic'' and scored a lot higher.</td>', 'Positive:Overall this is a fine photojournalistic capture worthy of publication. This image has strong emotion. The BG provides perspective and context to the image far, far better than most. Exposure is good and general photographic technical quality is fine. It gives the viewer much to think about. Is this the wrestler''s father happy at a victory? Is it a coach happy over his first ever state champion? It preserves a touching moment in time that can never be captured again which is a fundamental purpose of photography itself. Technicals:The BG is a strength. It clearly shows the context generating the reaction we see. Inclusion of the referee is very nice and it clearly shows the gym atmosphere of a wrestling competition. You are perfectly placed for the capture of the moment. That makes this a very fine image. Though exposure is good the overall lighting is nothing special. The capture of the moment is great, but the overall perspective has more in common with a snapshot than it does with fine art. The challenge:Right or wrong, voters in free study challenges are looking more for fine art images of exceptional technical quality than anything else. The ''snapshot'' perspective and lack of funk and flash post processing hurt this image in voting. When there are over 600 entries in a challenge with many being exceptional technical achievements it is easy for an image like this to be overlooked. It was. If you had surrounded it with a gradient like the three ribbon winners and applied some serious dodge and burn to hit the voter over the head with the embrace then it would have been more ''artistic'' and scored a lot higher.', '2007-03-09 11:46:27.000000', NULL, 0),
