(3448084, 477190, 63398, '<td valign="top">Svetlana.....I am so humbled by your amazingly elegant and inspiring talent. It''s a privilege to see you grow and get better with each day and photograph.</td>', 'Svetlana.....I am so humbled by your amazingly elegant and inspiring talent. It''s a privilege to see you grow and get better with each day and photograph.', '2007-03-10 05:18:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3448123, 473641, 57229, '<td valign="top">Let''s see now - Alfred Hitchcox was forever tilting the camera to bring out the oddity/scariness etc in a scene. Whether or not you intended that, it hasn''t worked here for me. I would have used the horisontal floors or the roof line for orientation and cropped to that. That''s one of my pet peeves though, so it may be worth ignoring.<br/>The area under arc lights is effectively blown out. I think that works against the theme of the picture. It''s good for the construction workers, but to put over the idea of night work in a picture, maybe it would be better that the work were more poorly lit, and the shadows more obscure.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=481695" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/57229/thumb/481695.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/57229/thumb/481695.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/57229/thumb/481695.jpg"/></a> <br/>There''s a little (exaggerated?) application of my thoughts there.<br/>I think it needs to be a little ''wrong'' to bring out surprise feeling you had (?) when you stumbled on the scene...</td>', 'Let''s see now - Alfred Hitchcox was forever tilting the camera to bring out the oddity/scariness etc in a scene. Whether or not you intended that, it hasn''t worked here for me. I would have used the horisontal floors or the roof line for orientation and cropped to that. That''s one of my pet peeves though, so it may be worth ignoring.The area under arc lights is effectively blown out. I think that works against the theme of the picture. It''s good for the construction workers, but to put over the idea of night work in a picture, maybe it would be better that the work were more poorly lit, and the shadows more obscure. There''s a little (exaggerated?) application of my thoughts there.I think it needs to be a little ''wrong'' to bring out surprise feeling you had (?) when you stumbled on the scene...', '2007-03-10 06:15:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3448160, 477021, 27482, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kablinki:</b></div><hr/><i> Definitely a photoshop deal, and not a very good one.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Dude, you got some imagination, I amire you for it and really look forward to seeing more of your photos in challenges cause if you can divert this much imagination on your own challenge entries, I think you should be up for a ribbon in no time :)</td>', 'Originally posted by kablinki: Definitely a photoshop deal, and not a very good one.  Dude, you got some imagination, I amire you for it and really look forward to seeing more of your photos in challenges cause if you can divert this much imagination on your own challenge entries, I think you should be up for a ribbon in no time :)', '2007-03-10 07:15:22.000000', NULL, 0),
