(3488388, 464490, 53147, '<td valign="top">Man - I need to start looking at what I choose as favorites after the challenge is over. I usually pick them so early in the challenge its like a surprise afterwards to see what I picked in my fave portfolio. <br/> <br/>I really liked this shot alot. The b&amp;w was great (though I wouldnt mind seeing the color version), but overall this shot just made me smile. I remember opening this up and just looking at it for a bit. Much longer than the many of the images in this challenge. This is just such a great capture of life and the growing lives of our little ones as they slowly turn into us. Great image Barry - and congrats on pic of the day. Well deserved.</td>', 'Man - I need to start looking at what I choose as favorites after the challenge is over. I usually pick them so early in the challenge its like a surprise afterwards to see what I picked in my fave portfolio.  I really liked this shot alot. The b&w was great (though I wouldnt mind seeing the color version), but overall this shot just made me smile. I remember opening this up and just looking at it for a bit. Much longer than the many of the images in this challenge. This is just such a great capture of life and the growing lives of our little ones as they slowly turn into us. Great image Barry - and congrats on pic of the day. Well deserved.', '2007-03-26 09:01:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3488727, 470696, 66384, '<td valign="top">As someone who has lived with a lot of depression around me, I don''t see it as the color red. (I think that effected my vote, which was 5.) I understand what you are saying about the pain, but somehow, red is too warm for depression. I see it much more as a cold tone. My husband has written some very insightful poetry about his depression, and much of it involves darkness and isolation and ice and snow.</td>', 'As someone who has lived with a lot of depression around me, I don''t see it as the color red. (I think that effected my vote, which was 5.) I understand what you are saying about the pain, but somehow, red is too warm for depression. I see it much more as a cold tone. My husband has written some very insightful poetry about his depression, and much of it involves darkness and isolation and ice and snow.', '2007-03-26 11:55:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3488900, 477090, 63269, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot - I love the smooth rich colors, and the shallow DOF - it makes the picture feel really sweet, which is fitting since the subject is so cute. :)</td>', 'Beautiful shot - I love the smooth rich colors, and the shallow DOF - it makes the picture feel really sweet, which is fitting since the subject is so cute. :)', '2007-03-26 13:24:10.000000', NULL, 0),
