(3490234, 462354, 39106, '<td valign="top">QxQ loses to NxP Checkmate, Qe4 loses to the same NxP. The Queen has to stay on the black diagonal to protect the c7 pawn.<br/>The correct move is Rf5, if white takes the free knight then rook down f1 is mate.</td>', 'QxQ loses to NxP Checkmate, Qe4 loses to the same NxP. The Queen has to stay on the black diagonal to protect the c7 pawn.The correct move is Rf5, if white takes the free knight then rook down f1 is mate.', '2007-03-27 00:52:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3490239, 462354, 50231, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jbchess1:</b></div><hr/><i> QxQ loses to NxP Checkmate, Qe4 loses to the same NxP. The Queen has to stay on the black diagonal to protect the c7 pawn.<br/>The correct move is Rf5, if white takes the free knight then rook down f1 is mate. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sweet I see that now thanks!</td>', 'Originally posted by Jbchess1: QxQ loses to NxP Checkmate, Qe4 loses to the same NxP. The Queen has to stay on the black diagonal to protect the c7 pawn.The correct move is Rf5, if white takes the free knight then rook down f1 is mate.   Sweet I see that now thanks!', '2007-03-27 00:55:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3490725, 476201, 24073, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous.  I wonder if some of the negative space on the left was cropped out, and the light was brighter, if it would make it more dramatic.  Its very cute, and nicely done.  One other thing I noticed, is right where Father and Son''s hands meet it seems to have some transparent stripes running horizontally.</td>', 'Gorgeous.  I wonder if some of the negative space on the left was cropped out, and the light was brighter, if it would make it more dramatic.  Its very cute, and nicely done.  One other thing I noticed, is right where Father and Son''s hands meet it seems to have some transparent stripes running horizontally.', '2007-03-27 09:48:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3494432, 473095, 69325, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by OmanOtter:</b></div><hr/><i> I can''t believe she''s a mother of two!  Wow!  She has a lot to be proud of to have such a body after two childbirths.  As for the picture, I really like it.  That particular shade of yellow against the black and white background is very eye-catching to me.  Her expression is wonderful - confident without being haughty.  And the flowing form of the sheet adds a VERY nice touch.  As for her breast and the tiny bit of vagina you can see, well, what''s wrong with that?  Anyone who votes down nudes just because they are nudes needs an attitude adjustment.  This is a very nice picture. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i think she would have to be in a much different position to see a tiny bit of vagina......</td>', 'Originally posted by OmanOtter: I can''t believe she''s a mother of two!  Wow!  She has a lot to be proud of to have such a body after two childbirths.  As for the picture, I really like it.  That particular shade of yellow against the black and white background is very eye-catching to me.  Her expression is wonderful - confident without being haughty.  And the flowing form of the sheet adds a VERY nice touch.  As for her breast and the tiny bit of vagina you can see, well, what''s wrong with that?  Anyone who votes down nudes just because they are nudes needs an attitude adjustment.  This is a very nice picture.   i think she would have to be in a much different position to see a tiny bit of vagina......', '2007-03-28 15:58:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3495561, 470505, 32997, '<td valign="top">you know there is something strange that I don''t know if I can explain...you found a nice moment, I like her smile (genuine), the tones are solid, as is the contrast...but I can''t help feeling she is in MY space, I like this woman but wish she would back up a bit...<br/>she has a nice big smile, and her eyes sparkle, but still too close...I can''t take this shot in, and I think in the end because it is fairly light, the shot fimply feels too tightly cropped...<br/>sorry for the lack of technical reasons or specifics, but that is my take...</td>', 'you know there is something strange that I don''t know if I can explain...you found a nice moment, I like her smile (genuine), the tones are solid, as is the contrast...but I can''t help feeling she is in MY space, I like this woman but wish she would back up a bit...she has a nice big smile, and her eyes sparkle, but still too close...I can''t take this shot in, and I think in the end because it is fairly light, the shot fimply feels too tightly cropped...sorry for the lack of technical reasons or specifics, but that is my take...', '2007-03-28 22:25:44.000000', NULL, 0),
